  "facts": [
    "The Jondal Tunnel, 10.4 kilometres long, opened on 7 September 2012, a day before the Prime Minister’s visit, marking a major milestone in Norway’s road network.",
    "Construction began in October 2009 and cost almost 806.6 million kr, a hefty investment that cut travel time between Bergen and Oslo by eliminating a lengthy ferry detour.",
    "For its first six years, the tunnel charged 100 kr for small cars and 200 kr for larger vehicles, before tolls were abolished on 8 June 2020."
